    seed_llvm_explicit_integer_to_f64_is_bitcast_2026-11-10, 0, "Actual c56 producer emitted literal 25.0/100.0 as raw bits 0x18/0x60; retained positive native probe exited14 at to-float-equality after digit control passed. Final diagnostic6 captured already-corrupt MirConstValue.Float payloads at backend entry, not a decimal serializer or runtime-string-parse defect."
    seed_llvm_explicit_integer_to_f64_is_bitcast_2026-11-10, 1, "Proven upstream owner: Rust seed LLVM compile_cast returns source_val unchanged for semantic I64-to-F64 Cast. c56 parse_float_int_part emits VMOVQ digit integer into XMM then VADDSD instead of CVTSI2SD; digit denormals accumulate raw25/100 before legacy float decode clears low bits."
    seed_llvm_explicit_integer_to_f64_is_bitcast_2026-11-10, 2, "Source candidate gates primitive integer-to-f64 conversion by semantic TypeId, restores signed/unsigned width and emits SIToFP/UIToFP; generic tagged/Any/text paths and ABI bitcasts remain unchanged. Independent source review and actual Rust component qualification PASS: baseline two intended width/conversion assertion failures, first GREEN compile failure preserved, corrected GREEN02 two exact x86/x64 LLVM IR and in-memory COFF tests PASS. Actual source3ae6 and retained executable0fb45; native fixture and constructor/descendant qualification remain pending."
    seed_llvm_explicit_integer_to_f64_is_bitcast_2026-11-10, 3, "Keep verification-pending after component IR/COFF tests until a rebuilt constructor produces a new pure-Simple compiler, actual Hello/numeric witnesses execute correctly, and dependent full CLI/test-runner qualification is admitted. No constructor/native-fixture/Phase3 exception or closed-bug claim is supplied by the current two-Rust-row diagnostic extension."

